### Complete RCE component checklist for offensive security research

An RCE vulnerability is rarely caused by one component in isolation. It usually occurs when untrusted input reaches a component that interprets, loads, compiles, deserializes or executes it.

For Android APKs, websites, APIs, Linux servers and Windows servers, these are the major components worth investigating.

### 1\. Operating-system command execution components

High priority

These components can execute operating-system commands.

| Component                   | Examples                                     |
| --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Shell interpreters          | Bash, Sh, Zsh, PowerShell, CMD               |
| Process execution APIs      | system(), exec(), popen(), subprocess        |
| Process creation            | fork(), execve(), CreateProcess()            |
| Script engines              | Python, PHP, Ruby, Perl, Lua                 |
| CGI handlers                | CGI, FastCGI                                 |
| Server-side include engines | SSI                                          |
| Task execution services     | Cron, systemd timers, Windows Task Scheduler |
| Remote management services  | SSH, WinRM, management agents                |

What to investigate: Whether attacker-controlled parameters, filenames, request values or uploaded content reach these execution functions without safe handling.

### 2\. Programming-language runtimes

High priority

| Runtime     | Components                                   |
| ----------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Java        | JVM, class loaders, reflection, JNI          |
| Android     | ART, Dalvik compatibility, DEX loaders       |
| Python      | Interpreter, eval, exec, import system       |
| PHP         | PHP-FPM, PHP interpreter, dynamic inclusion  |
| JavaScript  | Node.js, V8, browser engines                 |
| .NET        | CLR, assemblies, reflection                  |
| Ruby        | MRI, JRuby, dynamic evaluation               |
| Perl        | Perl interpreter, dynamic evaluation         |
| Lua         | Lua VM, native modules                       |
| WebAssembly | WASM runtime, module loader                  |
| Erlang      | BEAM VM                                      |
| Go          | Runtime, plugin loading                      |
| Rust        | Native libraries and unsafe interfaces       |
| C/C++       | Native executable and shared-library loading |

Investigate unsafe evaluation, untrusted module loading, runtime vulnerabilities and exposed native interfaces.

### 3\. File-processing components

High priority

| Component                    | What it processes                     |
| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| ImageMagick                  | Images                                |
| GraphicsMagick               | Images                                |
| FFmpeg                       | Audio and video                       |
| Ghostscript                  | PostScript and PDF-related processing |
| LibreOffice                  | Office documents                      |
| PDF processing libraries     | PDF documents                         |
| ExifTool                     | Image and media metadata              |
| Archive extraction libraries | ZIP, TAR, 7z and related archives     |
| XML parsers                  | XML, SVG and related formats          |
| Font engines                 | TTF, OTF, WOFF                        |
| OCR engines                  | Scanned documents and images          |
| Antivirus engines            | Uploaded files                        |
| Preview generators           | Images, documents and videos          |

A parser vulnerability can result in RCE when processing a malicious file. A file upload by itself does not prove that this is possible.

### 4\. Deserialization and serialization components

High priority

| Language/platform | Components and formats                       |
| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Java              | ObjectInputStream, Java serialization        |
| PHP               | unserialize()                                |
| Python            | Pickle, marshal                              |
| Ruby              | Marshal                                      |
| .NET              | BinaryFormatter and other serializers        |
| JavaScript        | Object reconstruction, unsafe object merging |
| YAML              | Unsafe object constructors                   |
| XML               | XML object binding and parser integrations   |
| JSON              | Custom object deserializers                  |
| Message systems   | Protobuf, Avro, MessagePack integrations     |

The key risk is reconstructing untrusted objects in a way that triggers dangerous behavior. OWASP identifies insecure deserialization as a possible direct RCE pathway. OWASP Web Security Testing Guide +1

