Investigate untrusted messages reaching unsafe parsers, deserializers, plugin handlers or command execution functions.

### 11\. Memory and native-code components

High priority

These are particularly important when researching native Android libraries, Linux services and Windows applications.

| Component or weakness                 | Potential consequence                                      |
| ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| Stack buffer handling                 | Stack buffer overflow                                      |
| Heap allocation                       | Heap corruption                                            |
| Use-after-free                        | Invalid memory access and possible control-flow corruption |
| Out-of-bounds write                   | Memory corruption                                          |
| Integer overflow                      | Incorrect allocation or bounds checks                      |
| Format-string handling                | Memory disclosure or corruption                            |
| Function pointers                     | Potential control-flow corruption                          |
| Virtual tables                        | C++ object-control corruption                              |
| JNI interfaces                        | Native memory vulnerabilities                              |
| Kernel interfaces                     | Kernel memory corruption                                   |
| Unsafe deserialization in native code | Memory corruption                                          |

These weaknesses do not guarantee remote exploitation. Network reachability, exploitability, architecture and mitigations matter. MITRE CWE documents many of these weaknesses. cwe.mitre.org +1

### 12\. Android-specific components

Important for APK research

| Android component      | What to investigate                         |
| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| DEX loader             | Dynamic loading of bytecode                 |
| DexClassLoader         | Loading external DEX/JAR code               |
| PathClassLoader        | Application class loading                   |
